---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { links } from "../data/links";
---

<Base title="Privacy – Parola" description="What Parola and this website do with your data.">
  <article class="narrow legal">
    <h1 class="t-title">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="t-lead">Parola is built to keep your recordings and transcripts on your Mac.</p>

    <h2>The app</h2>
    <p>
      Parola transcribes on your Mac. Your audio is never uploaded. There is no account, and Parola
      sends no analytics, crash reports or usage data anywhere.
    </p>
    <p>Parola connects to the internet only when you ask for something that needs it:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Downloading a speech model from Hugging Face. After that, transcription works offline.
      </li>
      <li>
        Fetching the audio behind a link you paste, with yt-dlp. The audio is downloaded to your Mac
        and transcribed there.
      </li>
      <li>
        Sending a transcript to an AI service you add yourself, such as OpenAI or Anthropic. Only
        the text is sent, never the audio, and Parola asks before the first time. If you route
        dictation cleanup to such a service, the context you allow for it (selected text, the
        clipboard or text on screen) is sent too. Apple Intelligence and Ollama answer on your Mac.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      macOS may download language files for Apple Speech and Apple Translation. That exchange is
      between your Mac and Apple.
    </p>
    <p>
      Parola keeps a short diagnostics log on your Mac for 7 days, capped at 10 MB. It holds no
      transcript text, file names or paths, and it never leaves your Mac unless you attach the
      report to a bug report yourself.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      This website sets no cookies and loads nothing from other servers. Its fonts and images come
      from this site too.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Write to{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${links.feedbackEmail}?subject=Parola%20privacy`}>{links.feedbackEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-block: clamp(56px, 8vw, 112px);
  }

  .legal .t-lead {
    margin-top: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 40px 0 12px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: -0.018em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  p:not(.t-lead),
  li {
    max-width: 38em;
    color: var(--ink-body);
  }

  p + p {
    margin-top: 14px;
  }

  ul {
    margin: 14px 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    list-style: disc;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--sage-deep);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>
